verses:
Waiting will not save me! Helpless, guilty, lost, I lie;
In my ear is Mercy‘s cry; If I wait I can but die;
Waiting will not save me.

Jesus wept and died for me, Jesus suffered on the tree;
Jesus waits to make me free; He alone can save me!

Faith in Christ will save me! Let me trust Thy weeping Son,
Trust the work that He has done; To His arms, Lord, help me run;
Faith in Christ will save me.

Jesus wept and died for me, Jesus suffered on the tree;
Jesus waits to make me free; He alone can save me!

items.lyrics:
Weeping will not save me! Though my face were bathed in tears,
That could not allay my fears, Could not wash the sins of years!
Weeping will not save me.

Jesus wept and died for me, Jesus suffered on the tree;
Jesus waits to make me free; He alone can save me!

Working will not save me! Purest deeds that I can do,
Holiest thoughts and feelings too, Cannot form my soul anew!
Working will not save me.

Jesus wept and died for me, Jesus suffered on the tree;
Jesus waits to make me free; He alone can save me!

Waiting will not save me! Helpless, guilty, lost, I lie;
In my ear is Mercy‘s cry; If I wait I can but die;
Waiting will not save me.

Jesus wept and died for me, Jesus suffered on the tree;
Jesus waits to make me free; He alone can save me!

Faith in Christ will save me! Let me trust Thy weeping Son,
Trust the work that He has done; To His arms, Lord, help me run;
Faith in Christ will save me.

Jesus wept and died for me, Jesus suffered on the tree;
Jesus waits to make me free; He alone can save me!

verses:
Let not conscience make you linger, Nor of fitness fondly dream;
All the fitness He requireth Is to feel your need of Him;
This He gives you, this He gives you, ʹTis the Saviourʹs rising beam.

Agonizing in the garden, Lo, your Saviour prostrate lies!
On the bloody tree behold Him! Hear Him cry before He dies;
“It is finished, it is finished!” Sinners, will not this suffice?

Saints and angels, joined in concert, Sing the praises of the Lamb,
While the blissful seats of heaven Sweetly echo with His name;
Hallelujah! Hallelujah! Sinners here may do the same.

items.lyrics:
Come, ye sinners, poor and needy, Weak and wounded, sick and sore,
Jesus ready stands to save you, Full of pity, love, and powʹr,
He is able, He is able, He is willing doubt no more.

Let not conscience make you linger, Nor of fitness fondly dream;
All the fitness He requireth Is to feel your need of Him;
This He gives you, this He gives you, ʹTis the Saviourʹs rising beam.

Agonizing in the garden, Lo, your Saviour prostrate lies!
On the bloody tree behold Him! Hear Him cry before He dies;
“It is finished, it is finished!” Sinners, will not this suffice?

Saints and angels, joined in concert, Sing the praises of the Lamb,
While the blissful seats of heaven Sweetly echo with His name;
Hallelujah! Hallelujah! Sinners here may do the same.

verses:
Out of my bondage, sorrow, and night, Jesus, I come, Jesus, I come;
Into Thy freedom, gladness, and light, Jesus, I come to Thee;
Out of my sickness into Thy health, Out of my want and into Thy wealth,
Out of my sin and into Thyself, Jesus, I come to Thee.

Oh, ʹtwas wondrous love the Saviour showʹd for me,
When He left His throne for Calvary,
When He trod the winepress, trod it all alone;
Praise His name forever, make it known.

All the way to Calvary He went for me, He went for me, He went for me;
All the way to Calvary He went for me, He died to set me free.

Could my tears forever flow, Could my zeal no languor know,
These for sin could not atone; Thou must save, and Thou alone;
In my hand no price I bring, Simply to Thy cross I cling.

I once was a sinner with turmoil within,
Condemned, trapped and powerless, living in sin;
But then my Lord came down and died on the tree,
Oh glory! Iʹm happy and free.

Now I am free! Forever free! Thus will my proclamation be;
Iʹm no longer bound by the shackles of sin! Oh glory to Jesus! Iʹm free!

I tried on my own to fight Satanʹs attacks,
With every step forward I fell three steps back;
But now I have Godʹs spirit living in me,
Oh glory! Iʹm fearless and free.

Now I am free! Forever free! Thus will my proclamation be;
Iʹm no longer bound by the shackles of sin! Oh glory to Jesus! Iʹm free!

Extol the Lamb of God, The sacrificial Lamb;
Redemption through His blood Throughout the world proclaim;

The year of jubilee is come! The year of jubilee is come!
Return, ye ransomed sinners, home.

The gospel trumpet hear, The news of heavʹnly grace;
And, saved from earth, appear Before your Saviourʹs face;

The year of jubilee is come! The year of jubilee is come!
Return, ye ransomed sinners, home.

Guide me, O Thou great Jehovah, Pilgrim through this barren land,
I am weak, but Thou art mighty; Hold me with Thy powerful hand;
Bread of heaven, Bread of heaven, Feed me till I want no more;
Bread of heaven, Bread of heaven, Feed me till I want no more.

items.lyrics:
Guide me, O Thou great Jehovah, Pilgrim through this barren land,
I am weak, but Thou art mighty; Hold me with Thy powerful hand;
Bread of heaven, Bread of heaven, Feed me till I want no more;
Bread of heaven, Bread of heaven, Feed me till I want no more.

Open now the crystal fountain, Whence the healing stream doth flow,
Let the fire and cloudy pillar Lead me all my journey through;
Strong Deliverer, strong Deliverer, Be Thou still my strength and shield,
Strong Deliverer, strong Deliverer, Be Thou still my strength and shield.

When I tread the verge of Jordan, Bid my anxious fears subside;
Bear me through the swelling current, Land me safe on Canaanʹs side,
Songs of praises, songs of praises, I will ever give to Thee,
Songs of praises, songs of praises, I will ever give to Thee.

verses:
I would have the Saviour with me, For I dare not walk alone;
I would feel His presence near me, And His arm around me thrown.

Then my soul shall fear no ill, While He leads me where He will;
I will go without a murmur, And His footsteps follow still.

I would have the Saviour with me, For my faith, at best, is weak;
He can whisper words of comfort That no other voice can speak.

Then my soul shall fear no ill, While He leads me where He will;
I will go without a murmur, And His footsteps follow still.

