I would have the Saviour with me In the onward march of life,
Throʹ the tempest and the sunshine, Throʹ the battle and the strife.

Then my soul shall fear no ill, While He leads me where He will;
I will go without a murmur, And His footsteps follow still.

I would have the Saviour with me, That His eye the way may guide,
Till I reach the vale of Jordan, Till I cross the rolling tide.

Then my soul shall fear no ill, While He leads me where He will;
I will go without a murmur, And His footsteps follow still.

verses:
Walking in sunlight, all of my journey,
Over the mountains, throʹ the deep vale;
Jesus has said “Iʹll never forsake thee,”
Promise divine that never can fail.

HeavenIy sunlight, heavenIy sunlight, Flooding my soul with glory divine;
Hallelujah, I am rejoicing, Singing His praises, Jesus is mine.

Shadows around me, shadows above me,
Never conceal my Saviour and guide;
He is the light, in Him is no darkness;
Ever Iʹm walking close to His side.

HeavenIy sunlight, heavenIy sunlight, Flooding my soul with glory divine;
Hallelujah, I am rejoicing, Singing His praises, Jesus is mine.

In the bright sunlight ever rejoicing,
Pressing my way to mansions above;
Singing His praises gladly Iʹm walking,
Walking in sunlight, sunlight of love.

HeavenIy sunlight, heavenIy sunlight, Flooding my soul with glory divine;
Hallelujah, I am rejoicing, Singing His praises, Jesus is mine.

