verses:
Not for case or worldly pleasure, Nor for fame my prayer shall be;
Gladly will I toil and suffer, Only let me walk with Thee.
Close to Thee, close to Thee, Close to Thee, close to Thee;
Gladly will I toil and suffer, Only let me walk with Thee.

Lead me throʹ the vale of shadows, Bear me oʹer lifeʹs fitful sea;
Then the gate of life eternal May I enter, Lord, with Thee.
Close to Thee, close to Thee, Close to Thee, close to Thee;
Then the gate of life eternal May I enter, Lord, with Thee.

items.lyrics:
Thou, my everlasting portion, More than friend or life to me,
All along my pilgrim journey, Saviour, let me walk with Thee.
Close to Thee, close to Thee, Close to Thee, close to Thee;
All along my pilgrim journey, Saviour, let me walk with Thee.

Not for case or worldly pleasure, Nor for fame my prayer shall be;
Gladly will I toil and suffer, Only let me walk with Thee.
Close to Thee, close to Thee, Close to Thee, close to Thee;
Gladly will I toil and suffer, Only let me walk with Thee.

Lead me throʹ the vale of shadows, Bear me oʹer lifeʹs fitful sea;
Then the gate of life eternal May I enter, Lord, with Thee.
Close to Thee, close to Thee, Close to Thee, close to Thee;
Then the gate of life eternal May I enter, Lord, with Thee.

verses:
Lord, my soul will wait for Thee, Fearless, blameless, here Iʹll stay;
Lord, Iʹm trusting only Thee, Lead me in Thy heavʹnly way.

He will guide me and care for me, Lead me onward to His sweet peace;
Lord, Iʹll watch and wait for Thee, In my sorrow, comfort me.

Lord, I pray, Thy Truth reveal, Guide me to the path above;
Thou my Saviour and my God, Show Thy mercy and Thy love.

He will guide me and care for me, Lead me onward to His sweet peace;
Lord, Iʹll watch and wait for Thee, In my sorrow, comfort me.

Lord, my life was filled with sin, Now at last I seek Thy grace;
Oh, remember not my past, And this sinner neʹer forsake.

He will guide me and care for me, Lead me onward to His sweet peace;
Lord, Iʹll watch and wait for Thee, In my sorrow, comfort me.

Lord, most gracious, most divine, Teach me now Thy righteousness;
That this lost sheep wilt Thou guide, And with meekness wilt Thou bless.

He will guide me and care for me, Lead me onward to His sweet peace;
Lord, Iʹll watch and wait for Thee, In my sorrow, comfort me.

items.lyrics:
Lord, my soul will wait for Thee, Fearless, blameless, here Iʹll stay;
Lord, Iʹm trusting only Thee, Lead me in Thy heavʹnly way.

He will guide me and care for me, Lead me onward to His sweet peace;
Lord, Iʹll watch and wait for Thee, In my sorrow, comfort me.

Lord, I pray, Thy Truth reveal, Guide me to the path above;
Thou my Saviour and my God, Show Thy mercy and Thy love.

He will guide me and care for me, Lead me onward to His sweet peace;
Lord, Iʹll watch and wait for Thee, In my sorrow, comfort me.

Lord, my life was filled with sin, Now at last I seek Thy grace;
Oh, remember not my past, And this sinner neʹer forsake.

He will guide me and care for me, Lead me onward to His sweet peace;
Lord, Iʹll watch and wait for Thee, In my sorrow, comfort me.

Lord, most gracious, most divine, Teach me now Thy righteousness;
That this lost sheep wilt Thou guide, And with meekness wilt Thou bless.

He will guide me and care for me, Lead me onward to His sweet peace;
Lord, Iʹll watch and wait for Thee, In my sorrow, comfort me.

verses:
Jesus, Saviour, pilot me Over lifeʹs tempestuous sea;
Unknown waves before me roll, Hiding rock and treachʹrous shoal;
Chart and compass came from Thee; Jesus, Saviour, pilot me.

As a mother stills her child, Thou canst hush the ocean wild;
Boistʹrous waves obey Thy will When Thou sayʹst to them, “Be still”;
Wondrous Sovʹreign of the sea, Jesus, Saviour, pilot me.

items.lyrics:
Jesus, Saviour, pilot me Over lifeʹs tempestuous sea;
Unknown waves before me roll, Hiding rock and treachʹrous shoal;
Chart and compass came from Thee; Jesus, Saviour, pilot me.

As a mother stills her child, Thou canst hush the ocean wild;
Boistʹrous waves obey Thy will When Thou sayʹst to them, “Be still”;
Wondrous Sovʹreign of the sea, Jesus, Saviour, pilot me.

When at last I near the shore, And the fearful breakers roar
ʺTwixt me and the peaceful rest, Then, while leaning on Thy breast,
May I hear Thee say to me, “Fear not, I will pilot thee.”

verses:
Jesus, Thy name I love, All other names above;
Jesus my Lord! Oh, Thou art all to me,
Nothing to please I see, Nothing apart from Thee, Jesus my Lord!

Jesus deepIy loves me, By His blood He bought me;
Jesus my Lord! Oh, how great is His love;
All other loves above, Love that I daily prove, Jesus my Lord!

The great Physician now is near, The sympathizing Jesus;
He speaks the drooping heart to cheer, Oh! hear the voice of Jesus.

Sweetest note in seraph song, Sweetest name on mortal tongue;
Sweetest carol ever sung, Jesus, blessed Jesus.

Your many sins are all forgivʹn, Oh! hear the voice of Jesus;
Go on your way in peace to heavʹn, And wear a crown with Jesus.

Sweetest note in seraph song, Sweetest name on mortal tongue;
Sweetest carol ever sung, Jesus, blessed Jesus.

All glory to the dying Lamb! I now believe in Jesus;
I love the blessed Saviourʹs name, I love the name of Jesus.

Sweetest note in seraph song, Sweetest name on mortal tongue;
Sweetest carol ever sung, Jesus, blessed Jesus.

His name dispels my guilt and fear, No other name but Jesus;
Oh! how my soul delights to hear The charming name of Jesus.

Sweetest note in seraph song, Sweetest name on mortal tongue;
Sweetest carol ever sung, Jesus, blessed Jesus.

