Lord, I believe Thou hast prepared, Unworthy though I be,
For me a blood bought, free reward, A golden harp for me!
A golden harp for me! A golden harp for me!
For me a blood bought, free reward, A golden harp for me!

There in a nobler, sweeter song, I’Il sing Thy power to save,
When this poor lisping, stammering tongue Is ransomed from the grave,
Is ransomed from the grave, Is ransomed from the grave,
When this poor lisping, stammering tongue Is ransomed from the grave.

verses:
Come let us gather with rejoicing, Praising our Lord in jubilant song;
For our beloved brother and sister, Love and devotion, sanctioned by God.
Lord, send Thy blessings, Lord, send Thy blessings; Help them to keep Thy word we pray;
Lord, send Thy blessings, Lord, send Thy blessings! O give them joy and peace always.

Let us all pray that God will lead them, And let them be in one heart and mind;
O let them honor God in their union; In joy or sorrow, comfort to find.
Lord, send Thy blessings, Lord, send Thy blessings; Help them to keep Thy word we pray;
Lord, send Thy blessings, Lord, send Thy blessings! O give them joy and peace always.

Let us pray that God will help them, Grow in the Spirit, ever and aye;
Fervently love Him, His presence seeking; Until that last most glorious day.
Lord, send Thy blessings, Lord, send Thy blessings; Help them to keep Thy word we pray;
Lord, send Thy blessings, Lord, send Thy blessings! O give them joy and peace always.

