verses:
Living for Jesus a life that is true, Striving to please Him in all that I do,
Yielding allegiance, gladhearted and free, This is the pathway of blessing for me.
O Jesus, Lord and Saviour, I give myself to Thee;
For Thou, in Thine atonement, Didst give Thyself for me;
I own no other Master, My heart shall be Thy throne;
My life I give, henceforth to live, O Christ, for Thee alone.

Living for Jesus who died in my place, Bearing on Calv’ry my sin and disgrace,
Such love constrains me to answer His call, Follow His leading and give Him my all.
O Jesus, Lord and Saviour, I give myself to Thee;
For Thou, in Thine atonement, Didst give Thyself for me;
I own no other Master, My heart shall be Thy throne;
My life I give, henceforth to live, O Christ, for Thee alone.

Living for Jesus thro’ earth’s little while, My dearest treasure, the light of His smile,
Seeking the lost ones He died to redeem, Bringing the weary to find rest in Him.
O Jesus, Lord and Saviour, I give myself to Thee;
For Thou, in Thine atonement, Didst give Thyself for me;
I own no other Master, My heart shall be Thy throne;
My life I give, henceforth to live, O Christ, for Thee alone.

