verses:
Just a few more days to be filled with praise, And to tell the old, old story;
Then, when twilight falls, and my Saviour calls, I shall go to Him in glory.
I’ll exchange my cross for a stary crown, Where the gates swing outward never;
At His feet I’ll lay ev’ry burden down, And with Jesus reign forever.

Just a few more years with their toil and tears, And the journey will be ended;
Then I’ll be with Him, where the tide of time With eternity is bended.
I’ll exchange my cross for a stary crown, Where the gates swing outward never;
At His feet I’ll lay ev’ry burden down, And with Jesus reign forever.

Tho’ the hills be steep and the valleys deep, With no flow’rs my way adorning;
Tho’ the night be lone and my rest a stone, Joy awaits me in the morning.
I’ll exchange my cross for a stary crown, Where the gates swing outward never;
At His feet I’ll lay ev’ry burden down, And with Jesus reign forever.

